sdrpp-p25 is free software under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (see LICENSE).
It links against the SDR++ core library (GPL-3.0).

Decoding is done by dsd-neo (https://github.com/arancormonk/dsd-neo, GPL-3.0), which runs as a
separate program and is not included here. dsd-neo uses mbelib-neo for IMBE (P25 Phase 1) and
AMBE+2 (P25 Phase 2) voice. Implementations of these vocoders may be covered by patents in some
jurisdictions; check the rules where you live before using them.

This software is for receiving only. Do not use it to decrypt anything, and respect the laws
on monitoring and on divulging the content of communications where you live.
